--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Components under their own terms
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The above covers picojet's own code. These parts came from elsewhere and keep
the licences they arrived with:

  Jet/                      The rasteriser, a submodule with its own LICENSE
                            file: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 CubeCoders Limited.
                            The MIT licence requires that notice to accompany
                            copies of the software, so a binary built from this
                            repository must carry it.

  picosdl/                  A submodule with its own LICENSE file, BSD-2-Clause,
                            covering in turn its own pio-st7789/ (BSD-2-Clause)
                            and pio-i2s/ (BSD-3-Clause) submodules and the
                            third-party material it lists.

  app/assets/               Generated by tools/convert_assets.py from meshes and
                            textures obtained elsewhere:

                              radio, column, biplane
                                  opengameart.org, CC0.

                              cube, f117, f22, efa, sphere, crab
                                  Shipped with the renderer from Gustavo Pezzi's
                                  pikuma.com 3D graphics course, and retained
                                  under whatever terms they arrived with.

The Raspberry Pi Pico SDK, which picojet builds against, is BSD-3-Clause and is
not distributed here.
